<h2>Members and visitors</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open <a href="/churches">Find a Church</a> on blessboard.com and select your congregation and branch.</li>
  <li>On your church site, use <strong>Member Login</strong> or <strong>Register as a Member</strong> when registration is open for that branch.</li>
  <li>For local ministry, events, giving, or membership questions, use the <strong>Contact</strong> page on your church site — your church administrators handle those requests.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Password help (members and church staff)</h2>
<p>Password reset is handled on your <em>church site</em>, not on blessboard.com itself:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Members:</strong> after opening your branch site, use the forgot-password link on the member login page (<code>/forgot-password</code> on your church hostname).</li>
  <li><strong>Branch administrators:</strong> use the forgot-password link on the branch administrator login page (<code>/branch/forgot-password</code> on your church hostname).</li>
  <li><strong>HQ administrators and ministry leaders:</strong> use the forgot-password link on the corresponding login page for your church site.</li>
</ul>
<p>Reset requests are reviewed by the appropriate church or platform administrators. If you cannot reach your church site, start again from <a href="/churches?for=admin">Church Administrator Login</a> or <a href="/churches">Find a Church</a>.</p>

<h2>Church administrators</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Start at <a href="/churches?for=admin">Church Administrator Login</a> on blessboard.com.</li>
  <li>Select your church and branch, then sign in on your branch administrator page.</li>
  <li>For branch operations training, use the handoff materials from your platform administrator when your church was provisioned.</li>
</ol>

